   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the tax law, in relation to creating a disabled person retrofit tax credit",
    "basePrintNo": "S2829",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S2829-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §606, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S2829\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the tax law, in relation to creating\na disabled person retrofit tax credit\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nTo provide an incentive for owners of residential buildings to\nretrofit homes for access to the disabled.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection One of the bill amends Section 606 of the tax law to allow a\ntaxpayer a tax credit to be equal to thirty percent, with a maximum of\n$5,000 dollars, of the cost of expenditures for retrofitting a home\nfor disabled access- Qualified improvements include:\n\n*A no-step entrance or entrance allowing access to the residence;\n\n*Interior passage doors providing at least thirty-two in wide opening;\n\n*Reinforcements in bathroom walls allowing installation of grab bars\naround the toilet, tub and shower; and\n\n*Light switches and outlets Placed in locations accessible to disabled\nPersons.\n\nThis credit shall be limited to one million dollars per year and will\nbe allocated among tax payers based on the order of the date of\nfiling.\n\n EXISTING LAW :\n\nNone.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nMany homeowners discover that retro-fitting homes to allow better\naccess for the disabled cost prohibitive and be deterred from making\nthe improvements. This legislation would provide a tax credit that is\nequal to thirty percent of the cost expenditures, up to $5,000 for\nmaking qualified improvements.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\n2015-2016: S.1388B - Amend and Recommit to Investigations and Gov't\nOperations\n2013-2014: S.1573A - Amend and Recommit to Investigations and Gov't\nOperations\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nTo be determined.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately and shall be deemed to have\nbeen in full force and effect on January 1, 2018; Provided further,\nthis act shall apply to all tax years commencing on or after January\n1, 2018.\n",
